From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] expose pinned S9+ ueventd rules at the M4 imported path

# Reason: M4 runtime ueventd imports missing /vendor/etc/ueventd.rc; Trustonic logs Permission denied opening admin device while its S9+ node rules exist only in /vendor/ueventd.rc.
# Affected: M4 runtime staging/verifier, boot_restore metadata and real ext4 verifier. Preserve hardware rule bytes and old path; no A37 hardware rules or daemon/readiness bypass.
# Verify: source hash, idempotence and destination-drift rejection, runtime self-test, full patch replay, actual device node permissions and Trustonic readiness/logcat; verify real ext4 bytes/UID/GID/mode/SELinux before packaging.
# Rollback: reverse this patch and rebuild; restore saved original BOOT/VENDOR after diagnostic device trial.

--- a/unica/patches/exynos9810_device_stack/exynos9810_boot_restore/a376b_android17_runtime_compat.py
+++ b/unica/patches/exynos9810_device_stack/exynos9810_boot_restore/a376b_android17_runtime_compat.py
@@ -17,6 +17,26 @@
 
